# Git: staging vs main

## Temporary override (2026-07-28 through 2026-07-30 inclusive)

**Prod-only window:** for Studio / Builder / platform control-plane, default working branch is **`main`** (not `staging`).

- When asked to commit/push/deploy these changes: commit on `main`, `git fetch` + integrate if behind, then `git push origin main`.
- Treat “deploy” as Vyom / `indobase.in` unless the user explicitly asks for staging/`indobase.fun`.
- Do not force-push. Production rollout still uses SHA tags on `.249` (see `indobase-prod-redeploy.mdc`).

From **2026-07-31**, ignore this override and follow the permanent rules below.

---

## Studio / Builder / platform control-plane

- Default working branch: **`staging`**.
- When asked to commit/push these changes: commit on `staging`, then `git push origin staging` (after `git fetch` + rebase onto `origin/staging` if it exists).
- Do **not** commit or push these to `main` unless the user explicitly asks to **promote to prod**.

## Production promotion

- Only when the user asks to promote, ship to prod, deploy to Vyom, or merge to `main`:
  1. Ensure staging smoke on `*.indobase.fun` is OK (or they explicitly skip).
  2. Merge/rebase `staging` into `main` (or cherry-pick as directed).
  3. `git push origin main`.
- Before pushing `main`: `git fetch origin` and integrate if behind (`git pull --rebase origin main`).
- Do not force-push `main` or `staging` unless explicitly requested.

## Other work

- Unrelated one-off branches only if the user names one.
- Marketing (`apps/www`) and infra-only docs may follow the user’s explicit branch choice; if unclear and it touches Studio/Builder deploy paths, prefer `staging`.
